  "description": "The 2026 election for Missouri's 8th Congressional District will determine who represents 30 counties across southeastern and southern Missouri in the U.S. House. Incumbent Republican Jason Smith, who has held the seat since 2013 and chairs the powerful House Ways and Means Committee, faces two Republican primary challengers and two Democratic primary challengers, plus a Libertarian candidate. The district has been reliably Republican for decades, but this cycle includes notable challengers including a former Democratic state senator who previously held the seat in the state legislature and a disabled Army veteran running on a progressive economic platform. The August 4 primary will narrow the field to one nominee per party for the November general election.",
